00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:06.080
So which is where SAP
Data Custodian comes in.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.820
SAP data custodian, there's a
little dashboard over there.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:14.390
It is a SaaS application
that we have developed.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.460
And the first phase
of this solution

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:18.320
is generally available.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:22.970
So I'll go a little bit deeper
into what this solution is.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:25.970
So before I go into that, we
have defined data custodians

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:29.030
to be responsible for the
implementation of business

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:32.270
rules that relate to the access
and protection of business

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:34.300
data.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:38.010
So as I mentioned, there are
two key phases of our solution.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:39.420
There is data
transparency, which

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:42.690
is generally available
which helps with monitoring

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:46.650
and reporting of data access,
storage, and movement,

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:49.840
and processing of your
data in the public cloud.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:53.610
So you will have more visibility
into how your data is accessed,

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.250
how it's stored, where
it's being moved,

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.670
and where it's being
processed in the public cloud.

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:01.470
And the data control
is our second part

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.210
of the solution,
which is going to be

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.360
available throughout
the rest of the year.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.460
We're working on that, so
we have a very robust policy

00:12:08.460 --> 00:12:11.160
engine that we have developed
out of Data Custodian.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:16.020
So an example for that would
