00:19:39.270 --> 00:19:41.970
Actually, before I do
that, let me show you

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:45.090
how to make a policy.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.880
So because the policy engine
is a very important part

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.790
of the solution.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:53.210
So I'm going to go and
see European union.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:58.360
So I will show you the--

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:04.230
so here to define a policy--

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:06.840
and this is something
that you can do--

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:10.190
is you're going to have
a name of the policy.

00:20:10.190 --> 00:20:15.120
You can have an action
of allow or deny.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.470
You will have an operation.

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:19.470
So the four operations right
now that we're looking into

00:20:19.470 --> 00:20:23.910
are access, placement,
movement, and processing.

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:25.900
You will have resource classes.

00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:28.320
So this is a very interesting
part of our policy engine.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:30.920
So either you can
say all my resources

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:34.960
in Google Cloud Platform, or
you can get more granular.

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.480
So you can either choose
it by resource classes,

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:41.700
so you can say all my virtual
machines or all my buckets.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:44.190
Or you can also be
even more granular

00:20:44.190 --> 00:20:45.990
and, say, choose
a specific bucket,

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:50.325
so that the bucket in Germany
with that German HR data

00:20:50.325 --> 00:20:52.200
might be something that
you can pick and have

00:20:52.200 --> 00:20:54.210
a specific policy for that.

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:58.440
So you choose how
granular you want to be.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.400
Now, you also have
to choose a location.

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:03.570
So is your data is
sitting in European union,

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.480
that's your resource location.

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:09.570
And now, this is actually
