accessed from the United

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:14.730
States.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:18.540
So I don't want all of my
data sitting in European union

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.230
to be accessed from
the United States.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.896
So that's something
that you can choose,

00:21:21.896 --> 00:21:25.310
and you can choose
other countries as well.

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:26.820
And you can choose--

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:29.050
so if it's access,
there two accesses

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:30.150
that we are monitoring.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:33.100
So it's your own customer
access, your own employee

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:35.630
access, as well
as Google access.

00:21:35.630 --> 00:21:37.660
So you can choose
either all, that you

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.900
don't want any of your access
from a Google support engineer,

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:44.320
or your own employee access to
happen from the United States.

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.230
Because you're concerned
about US regulation,

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:49.540
you're concerned that
under Patriot Act,

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:53.830
maybe the government is
going to somehow want

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:55.780
some of that data,
which is sitting--

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:57.670
and so that's why you
want to really keep

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:00.220
some of your data
defined and controlled

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.767
and not being accessed
outside of Europe.

00:22:03.767 --> 00:22:06.100
And that could be a good
reason why you want to do that,

00:22:06.100 --> 00:22:09.160
or you could have some other
technology or other reasons.

00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:10.690
And then you have
to define a risk

00:22:10.690 --> 00:22:14.980
level, which can be lowest,
low, medium, high, or highest.

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:18.811
And then that's a summary of
a policy that you would have.

00:22:18.811 --> 00:22:22.440
So going back to the
